<title>USA: Greyhound Lines Inc Sept passenger sales up.</title>
<headline>Greyhound Lines Inc Sept passenger sales up.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sept 1996     Sept 1995</p>
<p>  Passengers				 1,002	   1,022</p>
<p>  Passenger Sales			$33,219	  $32,988</p>
<p>  Passenger Miles			364,084	  369,982</p>
<p>Yield (Sales per Passenger Mile)</p>
<p>   (cents)				    9.12	     8.92</p>
<p>  Average Trip Length(miles)	     363		362</p>
<p>System-wide</p>
<p>  Regular Service Miles		 20,883	   20,482</p>
<p>  Available Seat Miles		 960,618	  942,172</p>
<p>					     Q3 1996	 Q3 1995</p>
<p>  Passengers				 3,657	   3,500</p>
<p>  Passenger Sales		     $128,887	$121,652</p>
<p>  Passenger Miles		    1,428,535     1,386,479</p>
<p>  Yield (cents)			     9.02	    8.77</p>
<p>  Average Trip Length(miles)	     391	     396</p>
<p>System-wide</p>
<p>  Regular Service Miles		 72,374	  71,362</p>
<p>  Available Seat Miles	     3,329,204     3,282,652</p>
<p>		   (in 000's except where noted)</p>
<p>NOTE: Statistics for sales generated by 198 largest locations represent about 72 percent of total monthly sales.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street Desk 212-859-1730</p>
</text>
